<title>HONG KONG: Northeast Elec 1996 net down 48.75 pct.</title>
<headline>Northeast Elec 1996 net down 48.75 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million yuan unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (yuan)		     0.096    vs 0.19 (see note)</p>
<p>    Dividend (yuan)		0.065    vs 0.065</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	    nil	vs nil</p>
<p>    Net				83.77    vs 163.46</p>
<p>    Turnover			 1,353.37 vs 1,451.21</p>
<p>    Company name		   Northeast Electrical Transmission</p>
<p>					 &amp; Transformation Machinery</p>
<p>					 Manufacturing Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		    May 6 to June 5</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	     June 21</p>
<p>NOTE - Northeast Electrical is China's largest high-voltage transmission equipment and transformer manufacturer.</p>
<p>The company gave no details on the calcuation of the share earnings. In 1995, the company reported an earnings per share of 0.23 yuan.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 0.065 yuan vs same.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
